description:
[claude] TC2 (RTEMS-2, lwIP 2.1.3 → 2.2.1 on rtems-lwip `tc2/upgrade-base-leon3`) is still hand-built. Because nothing declares what it withholds, `rtems/pkg/rtems-lwip` is deliberately left out of the KB crawl (ANVIL-39): its merge requests contain the upstream upgrade, i.e. the TC2 answer.

## Steps

* `cases/rtems-lwip-upgrade-2.2.1.toml`, kind `component-upgrade`:

  * repo `vishal7pandey/rtems-lwip`;
  * upstream reference commit(s) / MR(s) of the 2.2.1 import, under `[upstream]`;
  * base branch `tc2/upgrade-base-leon3` + overlay;
  * ticket = RTEMS-2's text;
  * `as_of`;
  * scoring: files plus the `#ifdef __rtems__` patch-marker gate.
* The loader accepts `kind = "component-upgrade"`. The scorer for this kind can come later; record it as a follow-up.
* Then add `rtems/pkg/rtems-lwip` to `KB_GITLAB_PROJECTS` and crawl it. Verify that a search for the upgrade MR returns nothing.

## Acceptance

* The case file loads.
* `python -m anvil.cases withheld` includes the TC2 MR/commits.
* rtems-lwip issues/MRs are in the KB without the withheld ones (counts posted).

Owner: claude. Size: M. Depends on: TC2 run 6 outcome (ANVIL-21) only for the scoring part.
